  "text": {
    "intro": "The Hollow Creek county fair runs its pie judging with more ceremony than the state legislature.\nFour bakers are involved. Determine each baker's placing, county and crust.\n- **Baker**: Winnie, Odette, Loretta and Caspian.\n- **Placing** (listed from better to worse): first, second, third and fourth.\n- **Home county**: Hobbs Bend, Fenwick, Quarry Hill and Ardmore.\n- **Crust**: a fork-crimped edge, a fluted rim, a crumb topping and a double crust.\nEvery baker has a different placing, county and crust, so within each category every item is used exactly once.",
    "clues": [
      "The baker who uses a fluted rim places third.",
      "First is exactly one place better than the baker who comes from Hobbs Bend, with no placing in between.",
      "The baker who uses a crumb topping and second are exactly one place apart in placing order, in one direction or the other.",
      "Loretta is better than the baker who comes from Fenwick in placing order.",
      "Winnie is exactly one place better than the baker who comes from Quarry Hill, with no placing in between.",
      "The baker who uses a fork-crimped edge is exactly one place better than Odette, with no placing in between."
